WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.360
- But speaking of balance
one thing I really did love

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.680
when I was reading your book,

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.170
and I could have used before now,

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.450
being in the midst of a divorce
is you really make a thing

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.101
about Sunday night
dinners with your family.

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:14.790
Y'all all get together and as a family.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.710
And it's so important, and
I actually remember my ex

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.810
and I, we tried so hard to do that.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.400
But you slip up, you know, you start.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.040
It's like, okay, well we skipped this one

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.680
because we had this important obligation,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.680
or we skip this one.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.500
And then sooner or later you miss them.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.027
You feel like that is kind of
a really important key thing-

00:00:32.027 --> 00:00:33.061
- [Jill] Absolutely.

00:00:33.061 --> 00:00:33.894
- That you and President Biden do

00:00:33.894 --> 00:00:34.727
to keep your family kind of sacred?

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:38.260
- Absolutely, and so we try to keep

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.440
the Sunday nights dinners.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.470
I mean, it's been a little busy
lately, but we still do it.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.010
And the kids look forward to it.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.530
And I think traditions really ground kids.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.920
And, you know, it was funny recently

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.370
my granddaughters has called
me and they said, Nana.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.220
You know, I'd love to have a
beautiful table with candles

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.180
and flowers or whatever
I can find to put on it.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.210
They said, Nana, we're
making our own dinner

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.410
and we're doing it Nana style.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.800
You know, we have our candles.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.243
And so some of it has permeated.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.340
I hope that they continue
on the traditions, too.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.840
- Absolutely, I think that
the biggest thing from that

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.950
is simply just saying you
matter to take this time.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.050
- [Jill] Sure.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.220
- I agree.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.320
How have traditions in general
really helped your family?

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.390
Like, 'cause now you have a daily,

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.300
isn't like a daily, you and
President Biden have dinner?

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.563
It's like date night now?

00:01:29.563 --> 00:01:30.396
(laughing)

00:01:30.396 --> 00:01:31.780
I love it, is it got like date night?

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.010
Like y'all have dinner every night?

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:33.843
- Yeah, we do.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:36.253
I mean, he's so busy, I'm so busy.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.240
But we do keep dinner.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.100
And we have dinner together, no phones.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.773
You know, the phones have to be off.

00:01:43.773 --> 00:01:47.630
And now we're having dinner
in this beautiful home,

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.890
and there's a fireplace in the dining room

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.890
and they light the fire and we just sit

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.050
and talk for a while.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.910
And then he has to go
back to work, you know

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.460
into the night, and I'm grading papers.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.680
- That sounded very The American President

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.822
with Michael Douglas and Annette Bening.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.253
(laughing)

00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:06.240
And I was very into it.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.270
How else do you unwind,
especially in such a tense job

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.860
and environment, how do you unwind?

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.560
- You know, I'm a big, I
mean, I love to exercise.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.130
- Oh I wish I did.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:21.130
- And I run, I bike, it clears my head.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.630
So that's really important to me.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.140
And I think all women
should have something.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.980
It doesn't have to be exercise,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.270
although hopefully it would be.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.340
- I wish it would be, Dr. Biden.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.190
- Just to take a moment
for yourself, you know.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:37.610
So I get up early and that's
my time that I have for myself.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.020
- I think all women, especially parents,

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.380
it has to be early because
if you don't do it,

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:42.540
if it's not the first thing you do-.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.629
- You lose the day.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.253
- [Kelly] It never happens, yeah, I agree.

